kerbridge (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=@URGENCY@

  Run `kbconfig upgrade` before you restart the daemon. It removes the
  retired sync.toml options cycle_deadline_seconds and read_deadline_seconds;
  the daemon refuses a file that still names either one.

  In idp_<source>.toml, admission_group and device_grant_group are removed.
  Set admission_group_id or device_grant_group_id to the group's Object Id
  (Entra, on the group's Overview page) instead of its name. `kbconfig
  upgrade` cannot make this change, and the daemon refuses a file that still
  names either old option.

  Delete /var/lib/kerbridge/sync/problem-admission-group-misconfigured*.json
  if it exists. Nothing clears it now.

  Delete /var/lib/kerbridge/sync/problem-graph-credential-*.json also. The
  two events are named sync-credential-expiring and sync-credential-expired
  now, so a problem left under the old name never clears. Change any
  monitoring rule that matches the old name.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  @DATE@
